{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A testimony</b> — Some say: the word belongs to עֵדוּת, like וַיָּקֶם עֵדוּת בְּיַעֲקֹב, even though it comes in masculine form, like וְדַעַת לְנַפְשְׁךָ יִנְעָם, for the tav is a sign of feminine. And some say: the vav belongs to חֹק לְיִשְׂרָאֵל, or to מִשְׁפָּט. And some say: עֵדוּת is like עֲדִי, like אֶת הַנֵּזֶר וְאֶת הָעֵדוּת, an allusion to the golden collar." "<b>When he went out over the land of Egypt</b> — Like וַיֵּצֵא יוֹסֵף, only we do not find Joseph in labors, but his foot was fettered with iron in prison. And some say: on Rosh HaShanah he went out from prison. And the correct view in my eyes: he mentioned Jehoseph with the addition of the letter heh of majesty, on account of the honored Name, and it stands for all Israel, as I mentioned in the psalm above." "<b>And the meaning of it being a statute</b> — On every new moon to blow the shofar, to recall the mighty acts of HaShem at the beginning of every appointed season and new-moon day likewise. Or he mentioned Joseph as standing for all Israel, in the manner of בְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב וְיוֹסֵף סֶלָה, as I explained there." "<b>When he went out over the land of Egypt</b> — When they came from Raamses and passed over the land of Egypt, and Egypt was burying their dead." "<b>And the meaning of 'a lip I did not know I would hear'</b> — Behold, the speaker stands for all Israel, who were required in Egypt to learn the Egyptian language, which their fathers did not know. And it should have been 'a lip that I did not know,' or the word 'with' is missing: 'with a lip of a people I did not know,' like the parallelism of בְּמִזְרְקֵי זָהָב אוֹ כֶסֶף יָיִן. And now he mentioned the statute that El placed in Israel, that He brought them out of Egypt, and this is: I removed his shoulder from the burden."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {4 "The phrase 'כדרך השותים במזרקי זהב' is unclear; rendered hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:50.483104861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}